IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg5, layer 1.
-- Sections 222 (notice of meetings and adjourned meetings), 229 (waiver of notice) and 230 (exception to requirements of notice).
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550).
-- It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Whether and when a notice was "given" is section 232 (module dg5-s232-s233-delivery-of-notice.l4); this module takes the day it was given as an input.
-- The record dates for notice and for voting are section 213 (piece dg4): taken here as facts about the person ("I was a stockholder of record on ...").
-- Section 114(b) does not carry section 222 over to nonstock corporations by the stockholder-to-member reading; section 230(b) names members itself.

§ `Section 222(a) -- what the notice of a meeting must say`

-- out of range: section 213(a) (piece dg4)
-- src:895 | (a) Whenever stockholders are required or permitted to take any action at a meeting, a notice of the meeting shall be given in accordance with § 232 of this title, and such notice shall state the place, if any, date and hour of the meeting, the means of remote communications, if any, by which stockholders and proxy holders may be deemed to be present in person and vote at such meeting, the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote at the meeting, if such date is different from the record date for determining stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting, and, in the case of a special meeting, the purpose or purposes for which the meeting is called.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(a) (src:895)
DECLARE `dg5 s 222(a) Notice of a meeting of stockholders` HAS
    `the meeting is a special meeting`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the meeting has a place`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `stockholders and proxy holders may be deemed present in person and vote by remote communications` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record date for voting differs from the record date for notice`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the place of the meeting`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the date and hour of the meeting`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the means of remote communications`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the purpose or purposes for which the meeting is called` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Each item is required only where it exists: the place, "if any"; the means of remote communications, "if any";
-- the record date for voting, "if such date is different"; the purposes, "in the case of a special meeting". The date and hour always.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(a) (src:895)
GIVEN n IS A `dg5 s 222(a) Notice of a meeting of stockholders`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(a) the notice of the meeting states what it must` n MEANS
        ((NOT n's `the meeting has a place`) OR n's `the notice states the place of the meeting`)
    AND n's `the notice states the date and hour of the meeting`
    AND ((NOT n's `stockholders and proxy holders may be deemed present in person and vote by remote communications`) OR n's `the notice states the means of remote communications`)
    AND ((NOT n's `the record date for voting differs from the record date for notice`) OR n's `the notice states the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote`)
    AND ((NOT n's `the meeting is a special meeting`) OR n's `the notice states the purpose or purposes for which the meeting is called`)

-- "Whenever stockholders are required or permitted to take any action at a meeting, a notice of the meeting shall be given".
-- src:895 | Whenever stockholders are required or permitted to take any action at a meeting, a notice of the meeting shall be given in accordance with § 232 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(a) (src:895)
GIVEN `stockholders are required or permitted to take action at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(a) a notice of the meeting must be given` `stockholders are required or permitted to take action at the meeting` MEANS
    `stockholders are required or permitted to take action at the meeting`

§ `Section 222(b) -- how long before the meeting, and to whom`

-- src:896 | (b) Unless otherwise provided in this chapter, the notice of any meeting shall be given not less than 10 nor more than 60 days before the date of the meeting to each stockholder entitled to vote at such meeting as of the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(b) (src:896)
DECLARE `dg5 s 222(b) Time allowed for a notice` HAS
    `the shortest time before the meeting that the notice may be given` IS A Period
    `the longest time before the meeting that the notice may be given`  IS A Period

-- "not less than 10 nor more than 60 days before the date of the meeting": both ends are inside the time allowed (Fork F1; section 213(a) is the model).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(b) (src:896)
GIVETH A `dg5 s 222(b) Time allowed for a notice`
`s 222(b) the time allowed unless otherwise provided in the chapter` MEANS
    `dg5 s 222(b) Time allowed for a notice` WITH
          `the shortest time before the meeting that the notice may be given` IS `period in days` 10
        , `the longest time before the meeting that the notice may be given`  IS `period in days` 60

-- "Unless otherwise provided in this chapter": another section of the chapter may fix a different time
-- (out of range: other sections of the chapter, several pieces). NOTHING means no other section applies, so 10 to 60 days stands.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(b) (src:896)
GIVEN `the time another provision of the chapter allows` IS A MAYBE `dg5 s 222(b) Time allowed for a notice`
GIVETH A `dg5 s 222(b) Time allowed for a notice`
`s 222(b) the time that applies to the notice` `the time another provision of the chapter allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time another provision of the chapter allows`
    WHEN JUST t  THEN t
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 222(b) the time allowed unless otherwise provided in the chapter`

-- NOTHING: the day the notice was given is not known to section 232 (that section does not make the notice effective), so this subsection cannot say.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(b) (src:896)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the time another provision of the chapter allows` IS A MAYBE `dg5 s 222(b) Time allowed for a notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(b) the notice was given within the time allowed` `the date on which the notice was given` `the date of the meeting` `the time another provision of the chapter allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the notice was given`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d  THEN
        JUST (    d AT LEAST (`the date` ((`s 222(b) the time that applies to the notice` `the time another provision of the chapter allows`)'s `the longest time before the meeting that the notice may be given`) `before` `the date of the meeting`)
              AND d AT MOST  (`the date` ((`s 222(b) the time that applies to the notice` `the time another provision of the chapter allows`)'s `the shortest time before the meeting that the notice may be given`) `before` `the date of the meeting`))

-- out of range: section 213(a) (piece dg4)
-- "to each stockholder entitled to vote at such meeting as of the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting".
-- The record date for notice is fixed under section 213(a) (out of range: section 213(a), piece dg4).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(b) (src:896)
GIVEN `the person was a stockholder on the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(b) the stockholder must be given the notice of the meeting` `the person was a stockholder on the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting` `the person is entitled to vote at the meeting` MEANS
        `the person was a stockholder on the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting`
    AND `the person is entitled to vote at the meeting`

§ `Section 222(c) -- an adjourned meeting`

-- out of range: section 213(a) (piece dg4)
-- src:897 | (c) Unless the bylaws otherwise require, when a meeting is adjourned to another time or place, (including an adjournment taken to address a technical failure to convene or continue a meeting using remote communication), notice need not be given of the adjourned meeting if the time, place, if any, thereof, and the means of remote communications, if any, by which stockholders and proxy holders may be deemed to be present in person and vote at such adjourned meeting are (i) announced at the meeting at which the adjournment is taken, (ii) displayed, during the time scheduled for the meeting, on the same electronic network used to enable stockholders and proxy holders to participate in the meeting by means of remote communication or (iii) set forth in the notice of meeting given in accordance with subsection (a) of this section. At the adjourned meeting the corporation may transact any business which might have been transacted at the original meeting. If the adjournment is for more than 30 days, a notice of the adjourned meeting shall be given to each stockholder of record entitled to vote at the meeting. If after the adjournment a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote is fixed for the adjourned meeting, the board of directors shall fix a new record date for notice of such adjourned meeting in accordance with § 213(a) of this title, and shall give notice of the adjourned meeting to each stockholder of record entitled to vote at such adjourned meeting as of the record date fixed for notice of such adjourned meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(c) (src:897)
DECLARE `dg5 s 222(c) Adjournment of a meeting` HAS
    `the bylaws require notice of the adjourned meeting`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were announced at the meeting at which the adjournment was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were displayed during the time scheduled for the meeting on the electronic network used for remote participation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were set forth in the notice of the meeting given under s 222(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the meeting that was adjourned`                            IS A DATE
    `the date of the adjourned meeting`                                     IS A DATE
    `a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote was fixed for the adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:897 | (i) announced at the meeting at which the adjournment is taken, (ii) displayed, during the time scheduled for the meeting, on the same electronic network used to enable stockholders and proxy holders to participate in the meeting by means of remote communication or (iii) set forth in the notice of meeting given in accordance with subsection (a) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(c) (src:897)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 222(c) Adjournment of a meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(c) the adjourned meeting was made known in one of the three ways` a MEANS
        a's `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were announced at the meeting at which the adjournment was taken`
     OR a's `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were displayed during the time scheduled for the meeting on the electronic network used for remote participation`
     OR a's `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were set forth in the notice of the meeting given under s 222(a)`

-- "If the adjournment is for more than 30 days": strictly more than 30 days, so an adjourned meeting held 30 days after the original is not caught (Fork F1).
-- src:897 | If the adjournment is for more than 30 days, a notice of the adjourned meeting shall be given to each stockholder of record entitled to vote at the meeting. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(c) (src:897)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 222(c) Adjournment of a meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(c) the adjournment is for more than 30 days` a MEANS
    a's `the date of the adjourned meeting` GREATER THAN (`the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` (a's `the date of the meeting that was adjourned`))

-- Notice of the adjourned meeting is needed when the bylaws require it, or the three ways of making the adjourned meeting known were not used,
-- or the adjournment is for more than 30 days, or a new record date for voting was fixed. (Fork F4: that the failure of the three ways means notice is required.)
-- src:897 | Unless the bylaws otherwise require, when a meeting is adjourned to another time or place, (including an adjournment taken to address a technical failure to convene or continue a meeting using remote communication), notice need not be given of the adjourned meeting if …
-- src:897 | If the adjournment is for more than 30 days, a notice of the adjourned meeting shall be given to each stockholder of record entitled to vote at the meeting. …
-- src:897 | If after the adjournment a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote is fixed for the adjourned meeting, the board of directors shall fix a new record date for notice of such adjourned meeting in accordance with § 213(a) of this title, and shall give notice of the adjourned meeting to each stockholder of record entitled to vote at such adjourned meeting as of the record date fixed for notice of such adjourned meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(c) (src:897)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 222(c) Adjournment of a meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(c) notice of the adjourned meeting must be given` a MEANS
        a's `the bylaws require notice of the adjourned meeting`
     OR (NOT (`s 222(c) the adjourned meeting was made known in one of the three ways` a))
     OR `s 222(c) the adjournment is for more than 30 days` a
     OR a's `a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote was fixed for the adjourned meeting`

-- "the board of directors shall fix a new record date for notice of such adjourned meeting in accordance with § 213(a)" (out of range: section 213(a), piece dg4).
-- src:897 | the board of directors shall fix a new record date for notice of such adjourned meeting in accordance with § 213(a) of this title, and shall give notice of the adjourned meeting to each stockholder of record entitled to vote at such adjourned meeting as of the record date fixed for notice of such adjourned meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(c) (src:897)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 222(c) Adjournment of a meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(c) the board of directors must fix a new record date for notice of the adjourned meeting` a MEANS
    a's `a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote was fixed for the adjourned meeting`

-- out of range: section 213(a) (piece dg4)
-- Who is owed the notice: "each stockholder of record entitled to vote at the meeting" (adjournment of more than 30 days),
-- and, after a new record date, "each stockholder of record entitled to vote at such adjourned meeting as of the record date fixed for notice of such adjourned meeting".
-- src:897 | and shall give notice of the adjourned meeting to each stockholder of record entitled to vote at such adjourned meeting as of the record date fixed for notice of such adjourned meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(c) (src:897)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 222(c) Adjournment of a meeting`
      `the person was a stockholder of record entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting as of the record date that applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(c) the stockholder must be given notice of the adjourned meeting` a `the person was a stockholder of record entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting as of the record date that applies` MEANS
        `s 222(c) notice of the adjourned meeting must be given` a
    AND `the person was a stockholder of record entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting as of the record date that applies`

-- src:897 | At the adjourned meeting the corporation may transact any business which might have been transacted at the original meeting. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 222(c) (src:897)
GIVEN `the business might have been transacted at the original meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 222(c) the corporation may transact the business at the adjourned meeting` `the business might have been transacted at the original meeting` MEANS
    `the business might have been transacted at the original meeting`

§ `Section 229 -- waiver of notice`

-- src:944 | Whenever notice is required to be given under any provision of this chapter or the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, a written waiver, signed by the person entitled to notice, or a waiver by electronic transmission by the person entitled to notice, whether before or after the time stated therein, shall be deemed equivalent to notice. Attendance of a person at a meeting shall constitute a waiver of notice of such meeting, except when the person attends a meeting for the express purpose of objecting at the beginning of the meeting, to the transaction of any business because the meeting is not lawfully called or convened. Neither the business to be transacted at, nor the purpose of, any regular or special meeting of the stockholders, directors or members of a committee of directors need be specified in any written waiver of notice or any waiver by electronic transmission unless so required by the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 229 (src:944)
DECLARE `dg5 s 229 Waiver of notice` HAS
    `the person entitled to notice signed a written waiver`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person entitled to notice gave a waiver by electronic transmission`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person attended the meeting of which notice was required`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person attended for the express purpose of objecting at the beginning of the meeting to the transaction of any business because the meeting is not lawfully called or convened` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A signed waiver (before or after the time stated) is equivalent to notice; so is attendance, unless the person came to object at the beginning
-- of the meeting that the meeting is not lawfully called or convened.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 229 (src:944)
GIVEN w IS A `dg5 s 229 Waiver of notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 229 notice is waived` w MEANS
        w's `the person entitled to notice signed a written waiver`
     OR w's `the person entitled to notice gave a waiver by electronic transmission`
     OR (    w's `the person attended the meeting of which notice was required`
         AND (NOT w's `the person attended for the express purpose of objecting at the beginning of the meeting to the transaction of any business because the meeting is not lawfully called or convened`))

-- "unless so required by the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws": the displaceable default of the core (Where a provision is made).
-- src:944 | Neither the business to be transacted at, nor the purpose of, any regular or special meeting of the stockholders, directors or members of a committee of directors need be specified in any written waiver of notice or any waiver by electronic transmission unless so required by the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 229 (src:944)
GIVEN `where the requirement to specify the business or purpose in a waiver is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 229 the waiver must specify the business or the purpose of the meeting` `where the requirement to specify the business or purpose in a waiver is made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the requirement to specify the business or purpose in a waiver is made`
    WHEN `in the certificate of incorporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in the bylaws` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in a resolution of the board of directors` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in none of these` THEN FALSE

§ `Section 230 -- exceptions to the requirements of notice`

-- src:948 | (a) Whenever notice is required to be given, under any provision of this chapter or of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of any corporation, to any person with whom communication is unlawful, the giving of such notice to such person shall not be required and there shall be no duty to apply to any governmental authority or agency for a license or permit to give such notice to such person. Any action or meeting which shall be taken or held without notice to any such person with whom communication is unlawful shall have the same force and effect as if such notice had been duly given. In the event that the action taken by the corporation is such as to require the filing of a certificate under any of the other sections of this title, the certificate shall state, if such is the fact and if notice is required, that notice was given to all persons entitled to receive notice except such persons with whom communication is unlawful.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(a) (src:948)
GIVEN `communication with the person is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 230(a) notice is not required to the person` `communication with the person is unlawful` MEANS
    `communication with the person is unlawful`

-- src:948 | and there shall be no duty to apply to any governmental authority or agency for a license or permit to give such notice to such person …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(a) (src:948)
GIVEN `communication with the person is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 230(a) the corporation need not apply for a license or permit to give the notice to the person` `communication with the person is unlawful` MEANS
    `communication with the person is unlawful`

-- "Any action or meeting which shall be taken or held without notice to any such person ... shall have the same force and effect as if such notice had been duly given."
-- The text says so only of the person with whom communication is unlawful: for a person who could lawfully have been reached it says nothing here (NOTHING).
-- src:948 | Any action or meeting which shall be taken or held without notice to any such person with whom communication is unlawful shall have the same force and effect as if such notice had been duly given. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(a) (src:948)
GIVEN `communication with the person is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 230(a) the action or meeting held without notice to the person has the same force and effect as if notice had been given` `communication with the person is unlawful` MEANS
    IF `communication with the person is unlawful` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:948 | In the event that the action taken by the corporation is such as to require the filing of a certificate under any of the other sections of this title, the certificate shall state, if such is the fact and if notice is required, that notice was given to all persons entitled to receive notice except such persons with whom communication is unlawful.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(a) (src:948)
GIVEN `the action requires the filing of a certificate under another section of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some persons entitled to notice are persons with whom communication is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 230(a) the certificate must state that notice was given to all persons entitled to receive notice except those with whom communication is unlawful` `the action requires the filing of a certificate under another section of this title` `notice is required` `some persons entitled to notice are persons with whom communication is unlawful` MEANS
        `the action requires the filing of a certificate under another section of this title`
    AND `notice is required`
    AND `some persons entitled to notice are persons with whom communication is unlawful`

-- src:949 | (b) Whenever notice is required to be given, under any provision of this title or the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of any corporation, to any stockholder or, if the corporation is a nonstock corporation, to any member, to whom (1) notice of 2 consecutive annual meetings, and all notices of meetings or of the taking of action by written consent without a meeting to such person during the period between such 2 consecutive annual meetings, or (2) all, and at least 2, payments (if sent by first-class mail) of dividends or interest on securities during a 12-month period, have been mailed addressed to such person at such person’s address as shown on the records of the corporation and have been returned undeliverable, the giving of such notice to such person shall not be required. Any action or meeting which shall be taken or held without notice to such person shall have the same force and effect as if such notice had been duly given. If any such person shall deliver to the corporation a written notice setting forth such person’s then current address, the requirement that notice be given to such person shall be reinstated. In the event that the action taken by the corporation is such as to require the filing of a certificate under any of the other sections of this title, the certificate need not state that notice was not given to persons to whom notice was not required to be given pursuant to this subsection.
DECLARE `dg5 s 230(b) Notices and payments returned undeliverable` HAS
    `notices of 2 consecutive annual meetings were mailed to the person at the address on the corporation's records and returned undeliverable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all notices of meetings or of the taking of action by written consent mailed to the person between those 2 consecutive annual meetings were returned undeliverable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of payments of dividends or interest on securities sent to the person by first-class mail during a 12-month period` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those payments returned undeliverable` IS A NUMBER
    `the person delivered to the corporation a written notice setting forth the person's then current address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a returned notice was given by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's electronic mail address appears on the records of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice by electronic transmission to the person is prohibited by s 232` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(b) (src:949)
GIVEN r IS A `dg5 s 230(b) Notices and payments returned undeliverable`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 230(b)(1) notices of two annual meetings and all notices between them were returned undeliverable` r MEANS
        r's `notices of 2 consecutive annual meetings were mailed to the person at the address on the corporation's records and returned undeliverable`
    AND r's `all notices of meetings or of the taking of action by written consent mailed to the person between those 2 consecutive annual meetings were returned undeliverable`

-- "all, and at least 2, payments (if sent by first-class mail) of dividends or interest on securities during a 12-month period ... returned undeliverable".
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(b) (src:949)
GIVEN r IS A `dg5 s 230(b) Notices and payments returned undeliverable`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 230(b)(2) all and at least 2 payments sent by first-class mail were returned undeliverable` r MEANS
        r's `the number of those payments returned undeliverable` AT LEAST 2
    AND r's `the number of those payments returned undeliverable` EQUALS r's `the number of payments of dividends or interest on securities sent to the person by first-class mail during a 12-month period`

-- Subsection (c): the exception in paragraph (b)(1) is not applicable to a notice returned undeliverable that was given by electronic transmission,
-- nor to a stockholder or member whose electronic mail address appears on the records and to whom notice by electronic transmission is not prohibited by section 232.
-- src:950 | (c) The exception in paragraph (b)(1) of this section to the requirement that notice be given shall not be applicable to any notice returned as undeliverable if the notice was given by electronic transmission. The exception in paragraph (b)(1) of this section to the requirement that notice be given shall not be applicable to any stockholder or member whose electronic mail address appears on the records of the corporation and to whom notice by electronic transmission is not prohibited by § 232 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(c) (src:950)
GIVEN r IS A `dg5 s 230(b) Notices and payments returned undeliverable`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 230(c) the exception in paragraph (b)(1) is not applicable` r MEANS
        r's `a returned notice was given by electronic transmission`
     OR (    r's `the person's electronic mail address appears on the records of the corporation`
         AND (NOT r's `notice by electronic transmission to the person is prohibited by s 232`))

-- Notice need not be given when paragraph (b)(1) applies (and subsection (c) does not take it away) or paragraph (b)(2) applies;
-- the requirement is reinstated if the person delivers a written notice of the current address.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(b) (src:949)
GIVEN r IS A `dg5 s 230(b) Notices and payments returned undeliverable`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 230(b) notice need not be given to the stockholder or member` r MEANS
        (NOT r's `the person delivered to the corporation a written notice setting forth the person's then current address`)
    AND (    (`s 230(b)(1) notices of two annual meetings and all notices between them were returned undeliverable` r AND (NOT (`s 230(c) the exception in paragraph (b)(1) is not applicable` r)))
          OR `s 230(b)(2) all and at least 2 payments sent by first-class mail were returned undeliverable` r)

-- src:949 | Any action or meeting which shall be taken or held without notice to such person shall have the same force and effect as if such notice had been duly given. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(b) (src:949)
GIVEN r IS A `dg5 s 230(b) Notices and payments returned undeliverable`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 230(b) the action or meeting held without notice to the person has the same force and effect as if notice had been given` r MEANS
    IF `s 230(b) notice need not be given to the stockholder or member` r THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:949 | the certificate need not state that notice was not given to persons to whom notice was not required to be given pursuant to this subsection.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 230(b) (src:949)
GIVEN r IS A `dg5 s 230(b) Notices and payments returned undeliverable`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 230(b) the certificate need not state that notice was not given to the person` r MEANS
    IF `s 230(b) notice need not be given to the stockholder or member` r THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
